{
  "_comment": [
    "The pkid and pki-httpd service definitions.",
    "",
    "Neither has a Triggers value, so installing the package starts",
    "nothing: a machine runs a certificate authority only once an",
    "administrator sets one up. `pki setup` (Set Up in the Certificate",
    "Authority window) provisions the machine and then adds Triggers=boot",
    "to both, never replacing a Triggers value already there.",
    "",
    "Both run under their own virtual service accounts (Identity Service),",
    "whose tokens authd makes, so both require authd. RequiredPrivileges",
    "names everything each keeps: peinit removes every privilege outside",
    "the list, and without SeChangeNotifyPrivilege a process can't",
    "traverse a directory. pkid also keeps SeAuditPrivilege, which lets it",
    "write its events (pkid.evman); pki-policy.reg grants both to the",
    "service SIDs alone.",
    "",
    "Neither has a hook to make pkid's state directories: `pki setup`",
    "makes /var/state/pki and the folders in it, with their descriptors,",
    "before it turns pkid on, and pkid isn't started before setup. The",
    "SQLite database reads the attributes of each directory on its path;",
    "fsbase lets Everyone traverse /var/state, which includes that.",
    "",
    "RestartPolicy is OnFailure (1) and ErrorControl Normal (0): a machine",
    "boots without its certificate authority, and peinit restarts a",
    "service that fails.",
    "",
    "Readiness is Notify (0): pkid notifies once its socket is listening,",
    "even while its configuration is invalid, so that it can say what is",
    "wrong; pki-httpd once it is listening on its port.",
    "",
    "Shipped by the pki package into /usr/share/regim/; inert until an",
    "image names it in [registry] autoapply."
  ],
  "keys": [
    { "path": "Machine\\System" },
    { "path": "Machine\\System\\Services" },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\pkid",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath", "type": "sz", "data": "/usr/sbin/pkid" },
        { "name": "Identity", "type": "sz", "data": "Service" },
        {
          "name": "RequiredPrivileges",
          "type": "multi",
          "data": ["SeChangeNotifyPrivilege", "SeAuditPrivilege"]
        },
        { "name": "Requires", "type": "multi", "data": ["authd"] },
        { "name": "Readiness", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "RuntimeDirectories", "type": "multi", "data": ["pkid"] },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy", "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "DisplayName", "type": "sz", "data": "Certificate Service" },
        {
          "name": "Description",
          "type": "sz",
          "data": "Issues and revokes certificates for this machine's certificate authorities"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": "Machine\\System\\Services\\pki-httpd",
      "values": [
        { "name": "ImagePath", "type": "sz", "data": "/usr/sbin/pki-httpd" },
        { "name": "Identity", "type": "sz", "data": "Service" },
        { "name": "RequiredPrivileges", "type": "multi", "data": ["SeChangeNotifyPrivilege"] },
        { "name": "Requires", "type": "multi", "data": ["authd"] },
        { "name": "Readiness", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "RuntimeDirectories", "type": "multi", "data": ["pki-httpd"] },
        { "name": "RestartPolicy", "type": "dword", "data": 1 },
        { "name": "ErrorControl", "type": "dword", "data": 0 },
        { "name": "DisplayName", "type": "sz", "data": "Revocation Publishing" },
        {
          "name": "Description",
          "type": "sz",
          "data": "Serves the certificate authorities' revocation lists over HTTP"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
